    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "Uses the four local macros below as a reusable function library.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 9/9: REUSABLE MACROS (a function library)\nA macro is a named sub-graph with its own inputs and outputs (see the tabs at the top of the editor: Main plus\none tab per macro; open them to read their bodies). Instances behave like ordinary nodes, but each one is\nEXPANDED into the caller at compile time, so macros can use exec flow, latent nodes and hidden state\n(a Do Once or Delay inside a macro is separate for every instance). Library macros (Content Browser >\nMacro Library) share macros between classes; the four here are local to this class.\nMacros vs custom events: a custom event is called by name, can be latent and is visible to the world; a macro\nis inlined and is for reusable flow shapes.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -360
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          260
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. USING MACROS - PrintTagged logs with a uniform prefix (its `tag` and `message` are typed into the\ninstance's pins). ClampedAdd then adds `heal_amount` to `health` but never beyond `max_health`:\n95 + 20 stays 100. Macro nodes show their input pins on the left and outputs on the right like built-in\nnodes; exec pins are named by the macro author (`then`).",
        "position": [
          -30,
          -70
        ],
        "size": [
          2360,
          940
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "m_tag",
          "m_hp",
          "m_heal",
          "m_cap",
          "m_clamp",
          "m_set",
          "m_cat",
          "m_tag2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. DEBOUNCE MACRO - any key press runs the Debounce macro; its output fires only after `debounce_ms` of\nquiet. A named macro makes the intent readable where a bare Retriggerable Delay would not.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          1080
        ],
        "size": [
          1000,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "kd",
          "d_db",
          "d_ms",
          "d_tag"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. A MACRO WITH A BODY WIRE - Repeat exposes the `body` exec output, like a For Loop: spawn one object per\niteration. `spawn_count` is a variable so designers tune it per instance.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          1770
        ],
        "size": [
          1000,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "rp",
          "r_n",
          "r_rep",
          "r_spawn"
        ]
      }
    ],
